<title>SPAIN: Spain to save 200 bln pta in fighting fraud - Aznar.</title>
<headline>Spain to save 200 bln pta in fighting fraud - Aznar.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Prime Minister Jose Maria Aznar said on Wednesday Spain could save more than 200 billion pesetas ($1.4 billion) this year through its fight against social security fraud.</p>
<p>&quot;The approval of a plan to fight social security fraud allowed a 1996 saving of around 88 billion pesetas and we hope to save more than 200 billion pesetas this year,&quot; Aznar said in his opening speech of in a debate on the state of the nation.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
</text>
